From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:15:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock Chrome close watcher and document PiP surfaces

Fill the two missing interfaces in benchmark's chrome-window-features
assertion without adding a renderer, OS window backend or platform close
request manager. Keep the mocked interfaces together in CloseWatcher.zig
and reuse native EventTarget, media_events and bridge bindings.

CloseWatcher exposes requestClose/close/destroy and cancel/close handlers,
with reentrancy guards and idempotent destruction. A JS-owned signal edge
keeps AbortSignal alive; checking its state on programmatic close requests
models silent abort destruction without a new native subscription system.
The passive mock has no history-action activation, so cancel events are
non-cancelable. There is no Escape/back-button or dialog/popover integration.

DocumentPictureInPicture is a secure-context Window singleton with an idle
null window, onenter and requestWindow. Convert options in Web IDL order,
enforce dimension ranges and preserve getter exceptions as Promise
rejections. Valid requests reject with a NotAllowedError DOMException;
user-activated successful PiP windows are deliberately not simulated.
Expose the companion event with its required Window payload. Capture native
exposure descriptors before scripts run and restore them on origin changes
without rereading page-controlled Window/Object globals.

Validation: ReleaseFast build; 1658/1658 existing upstream tests; 100
checks in ignored temporary secure/insecure diagnostics covering default
constructors, forced GC, event order, abort, worker exposure, singleton
identity, option conversion, Promise rejections and poisoned Window getter.
The unmodified benchmark improves from 124/130 to 125/130 (96.15%), with
chrome-window-features newly passing and no previous pass regressing.
No unit tests or benchmark source changes are added.

References:
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#the-closewatcher-interface
https://wicg.github.io/document-picture-in-picture/
